# SizeKit — Architecture Constraints

## Forbidden unless product owner explicitly approves

- Backend, database, user accounts, cloud storage, server-side processing
- Firebase, Supabase, AWS, Vercel backends, Cloudinary, ImageKit, Uploadcare
- Any paid image-processing or paid AI API (OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, etc.)
- Recurring infrastructure or SaaS costs

## Required

- Core features work offline on-device
- Prefer Expo/RN APIs, open-source libs, deterministic local algorithms
- Never upload user files; never log image contents
- Clean up temp files; handle permissions with clear explanations
- Presets live in structured config (not hardcoded official claims without verification)

```typescript
interface RequirementPreset {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  category: string;
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
  maxFileSizeBytes?: number;
  allowedFormats?: string[];
  description?: string;
}
```

## Differentiator

Exact target file size (e.g. 200 KB) without manual JPEG-quality tinkering. If exact size is impossible, return closest practical result and explain clearly.
